# Dependencies
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# Build output
dist/
build/

# Tauri / Rust
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/schemas/

# `src-tauri/Cargo.lock` is deliberately **not** ignored. ART is an
# application, not a library, so the lockfile is part of what it ships: it is
# what makes a build reproducible and what `cargo deny check` actually checks.
# That mattered less while every dependency was permissive and pinned by hand;
# it started mattering on 2026-08-16, when `libpfs3` arrived as the first
# copyleft dependency inside `core/` and brought a transitive set with it.
# Auditing an unlocked tree tells you about whatever resolved that morning.

# Logs
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

